Ours (dsv41 recipe), Apache-2.0, against vLLM main 6e517b15 + patches 0001-0021 + 0023-0027 (touches engram.py only).
Engram's wkv row-parallel over the hash heads (VLLM_ENGRAM_WKV_ROWPAR=1, default off, the same on every rank). Each
decode step, per Engram layer (1 and 14), a TP rank looks up its own contiguous share of the 24 hash heads (12 at
TP=2), embed() all-gathers the rows (60-261 us), the column-parallel wkv (6144 -> 25600, MXFP8 on Marlin, 363-395 us)
multiplies the gathered rows by the rank's output columns, and its output is all-gathered again (45-73 us). The gathered
rows are head-major, so a rank's own heads are exactly wkv's input-row shard (columns [rank * 3072, (rank + 1) * 3072)
at TP=2): with the flag, wkv is a RowParallelLinear over them, embed() hands it the rank's staged rows ungathered, and
one all-reduce of the [tokens, 25600] partial products replaces both all-gathers, at the same FLOPs and weight bytes a
rank. TensorFold runs this layout at ~0.55 ms a round for both layers against our 1.05-1.17 ms; the layout alone should
be worth 0.25-0.35 ms a round. No loader change: vLLM's RowParallelLinear loaders cut the checkpoint tensors by input
rows (MXFP8: weight [25600, 3072] e4m3, the [32, 32] ue8m0 block scales repeated to rows and narrowed on input_dim at
rank * 96 blocks; 128 x 128 FP8 blocks likewise), and the plugin's EXL3 engram.wkv takes its existing input-row cut
(whole 16-row trellis tiles, suh cut, svh whole). Engages for TP > 1 without sequence parallelism when TP splits the
heads into equal shares and the tables are not DP-sharded; otherwise a warning and today's layout, as with the flag
off or at TP=1. A rounding-class change, not bit-exact: each rank's partial is rounded to bf16 before the cross-rank
sum (at 6 rows 37% of outputs move, by at most 2 ulps of the larger partial; norm-wise error 1.48x today's), so greedy
text can move at near-ties. Bytes: 51.2 KB of all-reduce a token a rank against 31.7 KB for the two all-gathers, so
prefill-sized steps move more; with the RDMA ring (EXL3_RDMA_AR=1) set EXL3_RDMA_AR_MAX_KB=1024, the 256 KB default
stops at 5 rows (a 6-row verify step is 307 KB). Row-parallel Engram is TensorFold's (github.com/bertholomus/TensorFold,
branch deepseek-v41-tp2, Apache-2.0); the code is ours. Tests: patches/tests/test_engram_wkv_rowpar_math.py (plain
torch, runs anywhere), patches/tests/test_engram_wkv_rowpar.py (serve image, GPU).

